---
title: "Columns Tool Panel - API"
enterprise: true
---

Control the Columns Tool Panel at runtime through its instance: show and hide sections, set a custom column layout, and expand or collapse column groups. The full list of tool panel parameters is in [Tool Panel Parameters](#tool-panel-parameters).

## Columns Tool Panel Instance

Get the Columns Tool Panel instance from the grid API using its tool panel `id`, which is `'columns'` by default:

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const columnsToolPanel = api.getToolPanelInstance('columns');
```

{% interfaceDocumentation interfaceName="IColumnToolPanel" names=["expandColumnGroups", "collapseColumnGroups", "setColumnLayout", "setPivotModeSectionVisible", "setRowGroupsSectionVisible", "setValuesSectionVisible", "setPivotSectionVisible"] config={"description":""} /%}

`setColumnLayout()` is covered in [Custom Column Layout](./tool-panel-columns-configuration/#custom-column-layout).

## Section Visibility API

Show or hide the Pivot Mode, Row Groups, Values and Column Labels sections after the grid is created by calling `setPivotModeSectionVisible()`, `setRowGroupsSectionVisible()`, `setValuesSectionVisible()` or `setPivotSectionVisible()`:

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
// hides the Row Groups section
columnsToolPanel.setRowGroupsSectionVisible(false);

// shows the Column Labels section
columnsToolPanel.setPivotSectionVisible(true);
```

The top area controls have no equivalent methods; they can only be removed through `toolPanelParams`. See [Section Visibility](./tool-panel-columns-configuration/#section-visibility) for an example.

## Expand / Collapse Column Groups

Call `expandColumnGroups()` and `collapseColumnGroups()` on the Columns Tool Panel instance to expand or collapse its column groups. Pass `groupId`s to target individual groups:

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
// expands all column groups in the Columns Tool Panel
columnsToolPanel.expandColumnGroups();

// collapses all column groups in the Columns Tool Panel
columnsToolPanel.collapseColumnGroups();

// expands the 'Athlete' and 'Competition' column groups in the Columns Tool Panel
columnsToolPanel.expandColumnGroups(['athleteGroupId', 'competitionGroupId']);

// collapses the 'Competition' column group in the Columns Tool Panel
columnsToolPanel.collapseColumnGroups(['competitionGroupId']);
```

To start with all column groups collapsed, set `contractColumnSelection` in `toolPanelParams` instead.

In the example below, `onGridReady` collapses all column groups in the tool panel. Use the buttons to try each call from the snippet above.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Expand / Collapse Column Groups" name="expand-collapse"  exampleHeight=640 /%}

{% note %}
The expanded column groups are saved and restored as part of [Grid State](./grid-state/).
{% /note %}

## Tool Panel Parameters

The Columns section and the [Column Chooser](./column-chooser/) use the same column selection panel. Their shared options are defined by `IColumnSelectionPanelParams`, while `IToolPanelColumnCompParams` adds options for the other Columns Tool Panel sections. See [Providing Parameters to Tool Panels](./side-bar/#providing-parameters-to-tool-panels) for how to pass these to the tool panel.

### IColumnSelectionPanelParams

{% interfaceDocumentation interfaceName="IColumnSelectionPanelParams" config={"overrideBottomMargin":"1rem"} /%}

### IToolPanelColumnCompParams

